  "provenance": "All six arms measure the merge 44416838 of dev c6bd08c6 into the #671 branch at c7d0ad63: the #671 firmware, whose shipping writer's boot judges each slot on one staged read under a three-read bound, compares two refused reads by their verdict, byte count, a CRC-32 over all but their last four bytes and those four bytes, and holds the writer when a slot's authority is unknown, with dev's capture harness, whose run.py applies the timing bound to production arms only, and dev's RTL. nvm_capture() and the census of #629 are unchanged. Processor pins 2ad2f845 (protocol) and 7dda9c3b (gPTP). All 96 captures repeat the system-cycle counts of the #671 round-5 receipt (bd42818d). The six arms ran in two drivers of three, so at most two builds ran at once; independent simulations overlapped. The capture SoC has no Milan MAC MDIO CSR, so the PHY path is compiled out. ARM through ATTEST contains no heartbeat or PHY call.",
